      "index": "b2C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 309516264,
      "version": 1819,
      "versionNonce": 1254216424,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1768919657963,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\n🧩 Background: Video Streaming\n\n\n1️⃣ Video Codec:\n\n→ Compresses & decompresses video, making it more efficient for storage\nand transmission. \n→ Abbreviation for \"encoder/decoder.\"\n→ Attempt to reduce size of video while preserving quality.\n→ Codecs usually trade-off on the following:\n        1) time required to compress a file,\n        2) support on different platforms, \n        3) compression efficiency (a.k.a. how much the original file is reduced in\nsize), and \n        4) compression quality (lossy or not).\n→ Popular ones: H.264, H.265 (HEVC), VP9, AV1, MPEG-2, and MPEG-4.\n\n\n2️⃣ Video Container:\n\n→ File format that stores video data (frames, audio) & metadata.\n→ Could contain info like video transcripts as well.\n→ Differ from codecs (codecs determine how a video is compressed /\ndecompressed, whereas a container dictates file format for how the video is\nstored)\n→ Support for containers varies by device / OS.\n\n\n3️⃣ Bitrate:\n\n→ Number of bits transmitted per second, kilobits per second (kbps) or\nmegabits per second (Mbps)\n→ Size & quality of video affect bitrate.\n→ High res videos with higher framerates (measured in FPS) have\nsignificantly higher bitrates vs. low resolution videos at lower framerates.\n→ Because more data requires to be transferred in order for the video to play\n→ Compression via codecs can also have an effect on bitrate (more efficient\ncompression leads to larger video being compressed to smaller size prior to\ntransmission)\n\n\n4️⃣ Manifest Files:\n\n→ Text-based documents that contain details about video streams\n→ 2 types of manifest files,\n        → Primary\n                → Lists all the available versions of a video (different formats)\n                → Acts as a \"root\" file, pointing to all the media manifest files\n        → Media\n                → Each represents a different version of the video\n                → Video is typically split into small segments, few seconds long\n                → List links to these segment files \n                → Used by video players to stream video by serving as an \"index\" for\nthe segments.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "DK5YRGJU2bOoWU3Oxpd_Z",
      "originalText": "\n\n🧩 Background: Video Streaming\n\n\n1️⃣ Video Codec:\n\n→ Compresses & decompresses video, making it more efficient for storage and transmission. \n→ Abbreviation for \"encoder/decoder.\"\n→ Attempt to reduce size of video while preserving quality.\n→ Codecs usually trade-off on the following:\n        1) time required to compress a file,\n        2) support on different platforms, \n        3) compression efficiency (a.k.a. how much the original file is reduced in size), and \n        4) compression quality (lossy or not).\n→ Popular ones: H.264, H.265 (HEVC), VP9, AV1, MPEG-2, and MPEG-4.\n\n\n2️⃣ Video Container:\n\n→ File format that stores video data (frames, audio) & metadata.\n→ Could contain info like video transcripts as well.\n→ Differ from codecs (codecs determine how a video is compressed / decompressed, whereas a container dictates file format for how the video is stored)\n→ Support for containers varies by device / OS.\n\n\n3️⃣ Bitrate:\n\n→ Number of bits transmitted per second, kilobits per second (kbps) or megabits per second (Mbps)\n→ Size & quality of video affect bitrate.\n→ High res videos with higher framerates (measured in FPS) have significantly higher bitrates vs. low resolution videos at lower framerates.\n→ Because more data requires to be transferred in order for the video to play\n→ Compression via codecs can also have an effect on bitrate (more efficient compression leads to larger video being compressed to smaller size prior to transmission)\n\n\n4️⃣ Manifest Files:\n\n→ Text-based documents that contain details about video streams\n→ 2 types of manifest files,\n        → Primary\n                → Lists all the available versions of a video (different formats)\n                → Acts as a \"root\" file, pointing to all the media manifest files\n        → Media\n                → Each represents a different version of the video\n                → Video is typically split into small segments, few seconds long\n                → List links to these segment files \n                → Used by video players to stream video by serving as an \"index\" for the segments.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
