    {
      "id": "zKlWpBebaBCsVfmflHExQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 878.2191608303117,
      "y": 3350.1951574742175,
      "width": 699.2394409179688,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 9545448,
      "version": 1920,
      "versionNonce": 1700712600,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1768919516209,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\n🔍 Common Video Codecs & Platform Support\n\n\n→ H.264 (AVC): The most universally supported codec across almost all\nplatforms, browsers, and devices, making it the standard for web video and\nstreaming.\n→ H.265 (HEVC): Highly efficient for 4K/HDR, but support is more\nfragmented. It is supported by default in Apple devices (iOS/macOS), and\nmodern Windows/Android devices.\n→ AV1: A modern, royalty-free codec supported by newer web browsers\n(Chrome, Firefox) and becoming more common in Android and high-end TVs.\n→ VP8/VP9: Developed by Google, widely used for web streaming (YouTube)\nand supported on all Android devices, browsers, and modern operating\nsystems.\n→ Apple ProRes: Widely supported in professional post-production\nworkflows within the Apple ecosystem.\n→ WMV (Windows Media Video): Primarily supported in Windows\nenvironments. \n\n\n🔍 Common Audio Codecs & Platform Support\n\n\n→ AAC (Advanced Audio Coding): Standard for Apple devices, YouTube, and\nwidely supported on Android and Windows.\n→ Opus: Open-source, low-latency, and high-quality; supported by WebRTC,\nbrowsers, and modern platforms.\n→ FLAC/ALAC: Lossless audio formats supported by most modern operating\nsystems and high-fidelity players.\n→ MP3: Universal support across all platforms. \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "WlSNSpEFGzqNVmxApPu_O",
      "originalText": "\n\n🔍 Common Video Codecs & Platform Support\n\n\n→ H.264 (AVC): The most universally supported codec across almost all platforms, browsers, and devices, making it the standard for web video and streaming.\n→ H.265 (HEVC): Highly efficient for 4K/HDR, but support is more fragmented. It is supported by default in Apple devices (iOS/macOS), and modern Windows/Android devices.\n→ AV1: A modern, royalty-free codec supported by newer web browsers (Chrome, Firefox) and becoming more common in Android and high-end TVs.\n→ VP8/VP9: Developed by Google, widely used for web streaming (YouTube) and supported on all Android devices, browsers, and modern operating systems.\n→ Apple ProRes: Widely supported in professional post-production workflows within the Apple ecosystem.\n→ WMV (Windows Media Video): Primarily supported in Windows environments. \n\n\n🔍 Common Audio Codecs & Platform Support\n\n\n→ AAC (Advanced Audio Coding): Standard for Apple devices, YouTube, and widely supported on Android and Windows.\n→ Opus: Open-source, low-latency, and high-quality; supported by WebRTC, browsers, and modern platforms.\n→ FLAC/ALAC: Lossless audio formats supported by most modern operating systems and high-fidelity players.\n→ MP3: Universal support across all platforms. \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
